### Description

**Observed Behavior**:
When attempting to scale up and create nodes with the kwok provider, we get the following error
```json
{"level":"ERROR","time":"2024-01-25T23:43:33.913Z","logger":"controller.provisioner","message":"creating node claim, NodeClaim.karpenter.sh \"default-ksfnj\" is invalid: [spec.requirements[0].key: Invalid value: \"string\": label domain \"karpenter.kwok.sh\" is restricted, spec.requirements[1].key: Invalid value: \"string\": label domain \"karpenter.kwok.sh\" is restricted]","commit":"eb8040d-dirty"}
```
**Expected Behavior**:
With default nodepool provided in kwok provider example  we should be able to provision kwok nodes without any modifications. 

**Reproduction Steps** (Please include YAML):

[This PR provides makefile command for repro](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/pull/967)

change the variables in `hack/create-aks.sh`, and `KWOK_REPO` in the makefile. 

After configuring the variables simply run `make az-kwok-all kwok-sample` to repro. 


** Nodepool and Workload**
Nodepool: https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/blob/0633cea638d2a3ec76ca63aca94ce5d289c30165/examples/kwok/default-nodepool.yaml
Workload: https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/karpenter/blob/0633cea638d2a3ec76ca63aca94ce5d289c30165/examples/workloads/inflate.yaml

Above are the workload and nodepool I applied via the makefile commands, also included the real yaml below of what it looks like after i ran ~/dev/karpenter-core (bsoghigian/kwok-failure-case*) » k get nodepools.karpenter.sh default -o yaml                                                                                

```yaml
